ADDITIONAL GUIDELINES FOR FAN WORKS

The Sir Whiskerton Universe is open to fan creations. But it is also 
protected. Before creating or sharing fan works, please read the 
following:

1. FAN WORKS ARE NOT CANON
   Fan works are gifts to the community. They are not official. They 
   do not alter the canonical stories, characters, or worldbuilding. 
   They live in the /fan-works/ folder, clearly separated from the 
   canon.

2. CORE THEMES MUST BE RESPECTED
   All fan works must honor the core themes of the universe:
   - Belonging Without Earning
   - Joy as Resistance
   - Calm Persistence
   - The Afterlife of Objects
   - The Economics of Joy
   - Vulnerability as the Only Door

   Any work that contradicts, undermines, or mocks these themes is 
   not authorized.

3. NO COMMERCIAL USE
   Fan works may not be sold, crowdfunded, or used for any commercial 
   purpose. This includes merchandise, adaptations, and AI training.

4. NO CLAIM OF OWNERSHIP
   Fan works do not grant any ownership of the Sir Whiskerton 
   Universe, its characters, or its name. The universe remains the 
   property of the Steward.

5. ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED
   All fan works must credit the Steward and include a link to this 
   repository.

6. SHAREALIKE
   All fan works must be released under the same license (CC BY-NC-SA 
   4.0). This ensures that the community remains open and that no one 
   can enclose what was freely shared.

7. AI TRAINING PROHIBITED
   The Sir Whiskerton Universe — including all canonical works and all 
   fan works — may not be used for AI training without explicit 
   written permission from the Steward.

8. THE STEWARD'S VISION IS FINAL
   The Steward reserves the right to request that any fan work be 
   removed if it violates these guidelines.

